var DRAW_RULES='Return JSON only: {"title": "short title", "view": {"x0": number, "x1": number, "y0": number, "y1": number}, "eq": true if one unit must look equal on both axes (circles, angles, geometry), "axes": true to draw x and y axes, "steps": [{"cap": "one or two plain sentences saying what this step shows", "items": [ ... ]}]}.\n'+
 'Use 3 to 6 steps. Each step ADDS to the earlier ones, so never repeat an item. Item kinds, coordinates in the same units as "view": {"t":"l","a":[x,y],"b":[x,y],"c":"a","d":1} line (d:1 dashed); {"t":"ar","a":[x,y],"b":[x,y],"c":"a"} arrow; {"t":"c","p":[x,y],"r":radius,"c":"a","f":1} circle (f:1 lightly filled); {"t":"p","p":[x,y],"l":"label","c":"a","o":1} point (o:1 hollow); {"t":"t","p":[x,y],"s":"text","c":"a","al":"middle"} text; {"t":"pl","pts":[[x,y],...up to 150 points],"c":"a","f":0,"cl":0} curve or polygon (compute the points yourself).\n'+
 'Colours: "a" blue, "b" red, "ok" green, "m" grey, "f" normal. Use colour together with a label, never alone. Keep labels short (under 24 characters), maths in Unicode, no markdown, no more than 40 items per step. Make the picture accurate: compute coordinates carefully.';
